    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d26e86e2_467cabb3",
        "filename": "common/system.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 953,
      "author": {
        "id": 1106949
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-06-02T19:26:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Then, I think a cleaner solution is to define HOOK_CHIPSET_SHUTDOWN_COMPLETE and call hook_notify(..._COMPLETE) from the end of POWER_S3S5 (just before return POWER_S5) or from POWER_S5G3. This should work for both x86 and sc7180.\n\nThis way, you can avoid impacting x86 projects (approaching releases) because only your project would react to SHUTDOWN_COMPLETE.\n\nHOOK_CHIPSET_SHUTDOWN doesn\u0027t seem properly named. It\u0027s more like SHUTDOWN_START. Calling handle_pending_reboot before completing a shutdown doesn\u0027t seem right.",
      "parentUuid": "a859fbaf_97adcb1d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 953,
        "startChar": 60,
        "endLine": 953,
        "endChar": 77
      },
      "revId": "15a80770291b67881e1cef35f02fa737c06d8b70",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b176b272_7f9e1d60",
        "filename": "common/system.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 953,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000407
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-06-02T22:47:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I thought of adding a new hook like this. But it seems overkilled just for this use case, as adding a new hook require extra flash and RAM.\n\nI\u0027d like to hear Paul\u0027s or other EC reviewer\u0027s opinion on the new hook.\n\nBTW, this is not only for Trogdor. All non-x86 boards (Rockchip, Mediatek, Qualcomm) behave the similar way: EC explicitly shutdown the power rails in S3S5.",
      "parentUuid": "d26e86e2_467cabb3",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 953,
        "startChar": 60,
        "endLine": 953,
        "endChar": 77
      },
      "revId": "15a80770291b67881e1cef35f02fa737c06d8b70",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
